╰┈➤𝗠𝘆𝗦𝗤𝗟 𝗖𝗼𝗻𝘀𝘁𝗿𝗮𝗶𝗻𝘁𝘀
A constraint is a rule applied to a table/column to control the data that can be inserted or modified
                                       Constraint = Data validation rule
Example: CREATE TABLE students (
    student_id INT PRIMARY KEY,
    name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    email VARCHAR(100) UNIQUE,
    age INT CHECK (age >= 18)
); -- Ikkada we've created several constraints

